{"path":"utility/program/SIG_strategies","title":"SIG_DFL, SIG_IGN","titleHtml":"SIG_DFL, SIG_IGN","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/program/SIG_strategies","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"The SIG_DFL and SIG_IGN macros expand into integral expressions that are not equal to an address of any function. The macros define signal handling strategies for std::signal() function.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/csignal\">&lt;csignal&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"co2\">#define SIG_DFL /*implementation defined*/</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"co2\">#define SIG_IGN /*implementation defined*/</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The <span class=\"t-lc\"><strong class=\"selflink\">SIG_DFL</strong></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><strong class=\"selflink\">SIG_IGN</strong></span> macros expand into integral expressions that are not equal to an address of any function. The macros define signal handling strategies for <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/program/signal\"><span class=\"kw980\">std::<span class=\"me2\">signal</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> function.\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Constant\n</td>\n<td> Explanation\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>SIG_DFL</code>\n</td>\n<td> default signal handling\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>SIG_IGN</code>\n</td>\n<td> signal is ignored\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/program/SIG_strategies\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>SIG_DFL</span>, <span>SIG_IGN</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/program","title":"Program support utilities"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"SIG_DFL, SIG_IGN","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. The SIG_DFL and SIG_IGN macros expand into integral expressions that are not equal to an address of any function."},{"label":"See also"}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":57,"codeBlockCount":0}
